{"type": "tool_call", "data": {"tool": "bash", "args": {"cmd": "cd /workspace/g-12; f=./downloads/rev_packedaway/packed\necho \"=== Try to read UBINT1 offset. First determine the UPX3 magic offset. ===\"\necho \"=== The program IS decompressing. The reason dump fails: at breakpoint OEP, decompression not complete. But actually the stub directly branches to 0x480860 - not a decompressed region. Let me understand the real layout.\nActually - static PIE UPX. The stub in PT_LOAD[1] (at 0x5000) runs and decompresses the main program into higher addresses which it mprotect+RX. The jump 0x2fb1c0 -> 0x480860 goes to the CRT which RUNS the decompressed program.\nSo by the time we hit 0x480860, decompression into 0x480000..0x560000 and 0x200000.. should be done. The 'Cannot access 0x49d000/0x2ec000' means those specific pages aren't mapped (perhaps holes between segments).\nLet me dump smaller contiguous ranges avoiding holes. Query mappings.\n===\"\ngdb -q $f -batch -ex \"set confirm off\" -ex \"starti\" -ex \"b *0x480860\" -ex \"continue\" -ex \"info proc mappings\" 2>&1 | tail -40"}, "call_id": "call_00_Sf9YBo1RpDV3NuDxZtp69316"}}
