{"type": "tool_call", "data": {"tool": "bash", "args": {"cmd": "cd /workspace/g-11 && python3 -c \"\nfrom pwn import *\nfrom capstone import *\nimport warnings\nwarnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\ne = ELF('./delulu')\n# disassemble the banner function 0x13f2-0x1449 and the ones at 0x1269 (error), 0x12ce(cls)\n# Analyze main logic thoroughly:\n# main: \n#   [rbp-0x40] = 0x1337babe\n#   [rbp-0x38] = &[rbp-0x40]   <- pointer to the int\n#   [rbp-0x30..-0x18] = 0 (buffer, 31 bytes read into rbp-0x30, i.e. read(0, buf, 0x1f))\n#   read(0, rbp-0x30, 0x1f)  <-- reads 31 bytes into stack buffer at rbp-0x30\n#   buffer spans rbp-0x30 to rbp-0x12 (0x1f=31 bytes). \n#   Compare [rbp-0x40] == 0x1337beef\n#   The buffer at rbp-0x30 is RIGHT BEFORE rbp-0x40... wait no\nprint('=== stack layout ===')\nprint('rbp-0x40: challenge int (0x1337babe)')\nprint('rbp-0x38: ptr to challenge (0x1337babe...)')\nprint('rbp-0x30: buffer start (read 0x1f=31 bytes)')\nprint('rbp-0x30 + 31 = rbp-0x11 ... that stays below rbp')\nprint()\nprint('KEY: buffer rbp-0x30 with 0x1f bytes -> up to rbp-0x11')\nprint('rbp-0x40 is at lower address than buffer! Buffer writes UPWARD go to -> rbp-0x11 max')\nprint('Hmm challenge at rbp-0x40 is BELOW buffer at rbp-0x30')\nprint('So to overwrite challenge at rbp-0x40, we need to write DOWNWARD past rbp-0x30...')\nprint('No wait: lower address = rbp-0x40, higher address = rbp-0x30')\nprint('buffer at rbp-0x30 grows UP to rbp-0x11. challenge at rbp-0x40 is BELOW buffer start')\nprint('=> cannot overwrite challenge from buffer overflow (buffer is above it)')\nprint()\nprint('BUT read(0, rbp-0x30, 0x1f) reads 31 bytes. That fills rbp-0x30 to rbp-0x11.')\nprint('No overflow of challenge int. So how to bypass?')\n\" 2>&1 | grep -v '^\\[*\\]'"}, "call_id": "call_00_5gjEGxq15ReX3IGiM8uy1107"}}
{"type": "tool_result", "data": {"tool": "bash", "call_id": "call_00_5gjEGxq15ReX3IGiM8uy1107", "result": "[*] '/workspace/g-11/delulu'\n    Arch:       amd64-64-little\n    RELRO:      Full RELRO\n    Stack:      Canary found\n    NX:         NX enabled\n    PIE:        PIE enabled\n    RUNPATH:    b'./glibc/'\n    SHSTK:      Enabled\n    IBT:        Enabled\n    Stripped:   No\n=== stack layout ===\nrbp-0x40: challenge int (0x1337babe)\nrbp-0x38: ptr to challenge (0x1337babe...)\nrbp-0x30: buffer start (read 0x1f=31 bytes)\nrbp-0x30 + 31 = rbp-0x11 ... that stays below rbp\n\nKEY: buffer rbp-0x30 with 0x1f bytes -> up to rbp-0x11\nrbp-0x40 is at lower address than buffer! Buffer writes UPWARD go to -> rbp-0x11 max\nHmm challenge at rbp-0x40 is BELOW buffer at rbp-0x30\nSo to overwrite challenge at rbp-0x40, we need to write DOWNWARD past rbp-0x30...\nNo wait: lower address = rbp-0x40, higher address = rbp-0x30\nbuffer at rbp-0x30 grows UP to rbp-0x11. challenge at rbp-0x40 is BELOW buffer start\n=> cannot overwrite challenge from buffer overflow (buffer is above it)\n\nBUT read(0, rbp-0x30, 0x1f) reads 31 bytes. That fills rbp-0x30 to rbp-0x11.\nNo overflow of challenge int. So how to bypass?\n"}}
