{"type": "tool_call", "data": {"tool": "bash", "args": {"cmd": "cd /workspace/g-14/extracted_maybe/rev_flecksofgold; echo \"=== Extract all entity names from rodata and decode as byte pairs ===\"\npython3 << 'EOF'\nd=open('flecks','rb').read()\n# entity names from rodata near 0xc54**\nnames_va_start = 0xc5465  # \"Explorer \" has a trailing space... let's grab names from the list region\n# The names: Explorer, Armanix, Ayaan, Brensom, Jaggex, Zavis, Austim, Randis, Aisaak, Antorn, Kartr, Charleagh, Desree, Brae[al]yn, Thalira, Kaelia, Allany, Adrian[nae], Catlea, Haylea, Celethe, etc.\n# Let's parse the continuous name list between \"Explorer\" and \"::\" terminator.\nraw=d[0xc546d:0xc5528+1]\n# Actually names are separated by \\x00. Let's split.\n# The byte-pair table r14 comes from Person name. But wait - the DISPLAY name and the byte-pair data may be the SAME array!\n# The lambda reads [r14+rbp*2] and [r14+rbp*2+1]. If r14=name string, and name is like \"Explorer\",\n# then pair0 = (0x45='E',0x78='x')?? No. Let's reconsider: maybe the name stores the pairs.\n# Hmm. Let me decode the name strings as sequences of (idx,char) pairs.\n# \"Explorer\" as bytes: 45 78 70 6c 6f 72 65 72\n# Pairs: (0x45,0x78),(0x6c,0x6f),(0x72,0x65),(0x72,...) - idx would be 0x45,0x6c,0x72 - too big for index.\n# That doesn't fit idx<0x50. So the byte-pair table is NOT the display name.\n\n# Reconsider: r14=[rbx+8]. Person struct [rbx]=Person, [rbx+8]=? In flecs, component Person might be just {int x; const char* tbl;}\n# OR perhaps Person is {name-pairs-array}. The .set<Person>({...}) in main passes the array.\n# Let me look at main to see the .set calls and find the actual byte table.\n\n# Let me look at main around entity creation. main@0x3af0. The lambda run at 0x5652? Actually main calls world.each at end.\n# The .set<Person> calls happen with immediate constant pointers. Let me disassemble main fully and look for set_.\n# Let me use capstone to disassemble main 0x3af0-0x5511 (before each).\nimport capstone\nmd=capstone.Cs(capstone.CS_ARCH_X86, capstone.CS_MODE_64)\nmd.detail=True\ntext=d[0x3510:0xc3fc0]\n# file offset 0x3510 = VA 0x3510. main VA 0x3af0 => file 0x3af0.\nmain_bin=d[0x3af0:0x5500]\nfor ins in md.disasm(main_bin, 0x3af0):\n    if 'lea' in ins.mnemonic or 'imm' in str(ins.op_str):\n        print('%08x  %-35s %s' % (ins.address, ins.mnemonic+' '+ins.op_str, '; imm'))\n    else:\n        print('%08x  %-35s' % (ins.address, ins.mnemonic+' '+ins.op_str))\nEOF"}, "call_id": "call_00_hl07uKRMzEB7ntdpo8MN6837"}}
