{"type": "tool_call", "data": {"tool": "bash", "args": {"cmd": "cd /workspace/g-21; python3 << 'EOF'\n# RSA params often stored as decimal in Go when using fmt to print, OR as raw hex. \n# The program reads moves, computes md5(moves) hex string. Then likely RSA-decrypts something.\n# The helper strings \"crypto/aes: invalid key size 45474735088646411895751953125\" - that 45... is \n# a decimal expansion that appears in a printf. Not useful.\n# Look for RSA params. In GlacierCTF rpgo, the verify likely: \n#   input moves -> md5 -> hex\n#   then treats something as RSA ciphertext, decrypts with private exponent d which is derived from moves?\n# Actually from writeup \"input maps to private exponent d\". So moves -> number -> d. Then d decrypts c.\n# n,e,c in binary. Let me find n (large, 1024+ bit) as a hex string stored in rodata.\n# Let me scan for all hex-ish strings (only 0-9 a-f) with length >= 48 (192bit).\nimport re\nf=open('extracted/rpgo','rb').read()\nfound=[]\nfor m in re.finditer(rb'[0-9a-fA-F]{48,}', f):\n    s=m.group()\n    # must not be preceded by hex char (not part of longer)\n    found.append((m.start(),len(s),s))\nprint(f\"hex runs >=48 chars: {len(found)}\")\nfor off,l,s in found[:50]:\n    print(hex(off),l,s[:60])\nEOF"}, "call_id": "call_00_5qDCMkKmqfC9HgOCbQBt8535"}}
