{"type": "tool_call", "data": {"tool": "bash", "args": {"cmd": "cd /workspace/g-21; python3 << 'EOF'\n# None of these is a clean ASCII hex RSA n. All the hex runs are embedded in decimal/error strings.\n# RSA params likely stored as raw bytes (big-endian) or as Go string/[]byte. \n# Let me search for raw byte runs that are large bignums: e.g., a pointer-size (4/8 bytes per limb) \n# little-endian data in .noptrdata, OR a contiguous raw big-endian sequence with first byte >= 0x80 \n# (large number, no leading zero). \n# Let me find contiguous runs of \"random-looking\" bytes (high entropy) of length >= 64 (512bit)\n# in the rodata/data (non-ASCII). Take any bytes with no ASCII printable and no common.\nimport re\nf=open('extracted/rpgo','rb').read()\n# scan for runs of bytes that are all in 0x00-0x1e or 0x7f-0xff (unprintable) >= 64 bytes\nruns=[]\ncur=0; start=0\nfor i,b in enumerate(f):\n    if b<0x20 or b>=0x7f:  # non-asciiish\n        if cur==0: start=i\n        cur+=1\n    else:\n        if cur>=64:\n            runs.append((start,cur,f[start:start+20].hex()))\n        cur=0\nif cur>=64: runs.append((start,cur,f[start:start+20].hex()))\nprint(\"raw non-printable runs >=64B:\",len(runs))\nfor r in runs[:80]: print(hex(r[0]),r[1],r[2][:40])\nEOF"}, "call_id": "call_00_TklB5sI5VE5xtfhe4CoX8909"}}
