{"type": "tool_call", "data": {"tool": "bash", "args": {"cmd": "CUURL=\"http://10.0.189.132:1337\"\n# The country whitelist is a STRICT equality match - trailing whitespace/newline/tab all rejected.\n# So country must be EXACTLY one of the whitelist strings. No injection via whitespace.\n# country route is dead. \n\n# Let me reconsider. The only flexible-looking field was description but it has ^[A-Z][a-z]{2,}$ regex.\n# Wait - does the description regex actually apply? Let me VERIFY. Earlier I assumed yes.\n# Let me test description with special chars directly via JSON.\n\necho \"=== Test description with hyphen (fails [a-z]? but has -) ===\"\ncurl -s -X POST -c /tmp/sess_g28.jar -b /tmp/sess_g28.jar \"$CUURL/addContact\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"firstName\":\"Test\",\"lastName\":\"User\",\"description\":\"Hello-world\",\"country\":\"France\"}' -w \"\\nHTTP %{http_code}\\n\"\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Test description with ${7*7} (SSTI probe) ===\"\ncurl -s -X POST -c /tmp/sess_g28.jar -b /tmp/sess_g28.jar \"$CUURL/addContact\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"firstName\":\"Test\",\"lastName\":\"User\",\"description\":\"ab\",\"country\":\"France\"}' -w \"\\nHTTP %{http_code}\\n\"\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Test description exactly 'ab' length 2 ===\"\ncurl -s -X POST -c /tmp/sess_g28.jar -b /tmp/sess_g28.jar \"$CUURL/addContact\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"firstName\":\"Test\",\"lastName\":\"User\",\"description\":\"ab\",\"country\":\"France\"}' -w \"\\nHTTP %{http_code}\\n\"\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Test firstName with special chars ===\"\ncurl -s -X POST -c /tmp/sess_g28.jar -b /tmp/sess_g28.jar \"$CUURL/addContact\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"firstName\":\"A<script>\",\"lastName\":\"Buser\",\"description\":\"Hello\",\"country\":\"France\"}' -w \"\\nHTTP %{http_code}\\n\""}, "call_id": "call_00_F5AdlLv1JTLPN5SOoNg16490"}}
