{"type": "tool_call", "data": {"tool": "bash", "args": {"cmd": "CUURL=\"http://10.0.189.132:1337\"\n# Reset session so we see only freshly-added contact.\nrm -f /tmp/sess_g28.jar\n# Add a contact with a distinctive value that would reveal th:text vs th:utext.\n# Best probe: a value that contains HTML that would only show if not escaped (th:utext),\n# but description is restricted to ^[A-Z][a-z]{2,}$. However firstName/lastName/description all same regex.\n# The distinguishing test for th:text vs th:utext with regex-limited values:\n#   Use a value where escaping matters. With pure letters there's nothing to escape, so we CAN'T distinguish.\n#\n# BUT - country whitelist ALSO only matches exact strings. All 4 fields are hard-restricted to benign strings.\n# => The contact fields CAN NEVER carry HTML/SSTI payload. So GET / rendering is irrelevant for SSTI.\n#\n# KEY REALIZATION: The pending idea (session persistence) claimed we could store malicious SpEL in session\n# via valid form, but NO valid form value can contain \"_\" or \"${\" or \"T(Runtime)\" due to regexes.\n# Therefore the pending idea gate (\"let malicious value pass validation and land in session\") is IMPOSSIBLE.\n#\n# => We must look for OTHER ways data enters session/template. Let me enumerate ALL endpoints & methods.\nfor path in \"/\" \"/addContact\" \"/contacts\" \"/api/contacts\" \"/api/contact\" \"/contact\" \"/list\" \"/contacts/list\" \"/api\" \"/health\" \"/error\" \"/favicon.ico\" \"/robots.txt\" \"/H2-console\" \"/console\" \"/webjars\"; do\n  for method in GET POST; do\n    code=$(curl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\" -X $method \"$CUURL$path\")\n    [ \"$code\" != \"404\" ] && echo \"$method $path -> $code\"\n  done\ndone"}, "call_id": "call_00_luJmzilYugmF7u3B4ITm9866"}}
