{"type": "tool_call", "data": {"tool": "bash", "args": {"cmd": "CUURL=\"http://10.0.189.132:1337\"\n# Observer instructed to verify th:text (escaped) vs th:utext (unescaped) rendering.\n# The rendered HTML shows \"Alice Cooper\" / \"Hello\" / \"United States\" as plain <p>, no Thymeleaf tags visible.\n# Distinguishing test: use a value containing HTML special char that would only survive as unescaped HTML.\n# Regex restricts to ^[A-Z][a-z]{2,}$ so we can't inject <>&. But we CAN still probe escaping via session data.\n#\n# BIG INSIGHT: The rendered contact had NO Thymeleaf attributes (no th:text or th:utext in HTML source).\n# The rendered block is:\n#   <p><strong>Alice Cooper</strong></p>\n#   <p>Hello</p>\n#   <p>United States</p>\n# This looks like processor output. If th:text was used, ${} in field would be literal text.\n# If th:utext or th:inline, ${} could be evaluated.\n#\n# Since no valid field can carry ${}, the test must determine the RENDERING MODE via the HTML source.\n# Let me look again - full HTML has NO th: attributes on the contact li. So this isn't a standard\n# Thymeleaf template with attributes; the server must be building HTML differently.\n# Let me test if thymeleaf INLINE is active by checking if the GET / controller returns a Thymeleaf template name.\n#\n# Actually - the cleanest test: add contact, then check if country whitelist has any \"seen in session, rendered unescaped\" leakage.\n# Since all fields are letter-only, escaping is untestable directly. \n# \n# Let me reconsider: maybe the vulnerability is NOT in the fields at all. Let me check for other HTTP surface:\n# OPTIONS/HEAD, springs error handling, and importantly whether 'description' is rendered through a SPEL/Template engine.\n# Let me probe the /error endpoint and template-resolver via view names once more with a different technique:\n# Spring Boot + Thymeleaf view-name SSTI via a fragment that echoes a request header/attr.\necho \"=== Test error page for stack trace / framework info ===\"\ncurl -s -c /tmp/sess_g28b.jar -b /tmp/sess_g28b.jar \"$CUURL/nonexistent-xyz\" -w \"\\nHTTP %{http_code}\\n\" | head -30\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Test error page rendering ===\"\ncurl -s \"$CUURL/error\" -w \"\\nHTTP %{http_code}\\n\" | head -40"}, "call_id": "call_00_2C2iOjxDS9KgIpUXnstU4334"}}
